        "detail": "Alan Jackson penned 'Where Were You When the World Stopped Turning' in the wake of 9/11, capturing the nation's grief and resilience. Recorded in a single day at the Sound Station studio in Nashville, the song's poignant lyrics struck a chord, earning Jackson a standing ovation at the CMA Awards. It's a testament to the power of music to heal and unite us in times of tragedy. Keep those memories close, and let's keep moving forward together, my friends."
